WEBVTT

00:00:57.750 --> 00:01:00.018
Alzheimer's disease
is the most common cause

00:01:00.042 --> 00:01:02.184
of dementia on the planet,

00:01:02.208 --> 00:01:07.768
affecting close to six million people
in the United States alone.

00:01:07.792 --> 00:01:11.309
But almost two thirds of all those people

00:01:11.333 --> 00:01:13.226
are actually women.

00:01:13.250 --> 00:01:16.018
So for every man
suffering from Alzheimer's

00:01:16.042 --> 00:01:17.643
there are two women.

00:01:17.667 --> 00:01:20.643
So why is that overall?

00:01:20.667 --> 00:01:22.018
Is it age?

00:01:22.042 --> 00:01:23.434
Is it lifespan?

00:01:23.458 --> 00:01:25.601
What else could it be?

00:01:25.625 --> 00:01:26.976
A few years ago,

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:28.934
I launched the Women's Brain Initiative

00:01:28.958 --> 00:01:31.226
at Weill Cornell Medicine
in New York City,